--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Getting Started</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/deploy\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Deployment</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/permissions\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Permissions</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/api-usage\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">API Usage</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><div class=\"VPSidebarItem level-1 is-link\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"item\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><div class=\"indicator\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"></div><a class=\"VPLink link link\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/operations\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\"><!--[--><p class=\"text\" data-v-eb85ecf7=\"\">Operations</p><!--]--></a><!----></div><!----></div><!--]--></div></section></div><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></nav></aside><div class=\"VPContent has-sidebar\" id=\"VPContent\" data-v-51608ad5=\"\" data-v-22444a1e=\"\"><div class=\"VPDoc has-sidebar has-aside\" data-v-22444a1e=\"\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><div class=\"container\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"aside\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"aside-curtain\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"></div><div class=\"aside-container\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"aside-content\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"VPDocAside\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\" data-v-871b5275=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><nav aria-labelledby=\"doc-outline-aria-label\" class=\"VPDocAsideOutline\" data-v-871b5275=\"\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\"><div class=\"content\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\"><div class=\"outline-marker\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\"></div><div aria-level=\"2\" class=\"outline-title\" id=\"doc-outline-aria-label\" role=\"heading\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\">On this page</div><ul class=\"VPDocOutlineItem root\" data-v-d607fa03=\"\" data-v-41a17517=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--></ul></div></nav><!--[--><!--]--><div class=\"spacer\" data-v-871b5275=\"\"></div><!--[--><!--]--><!----><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class=\"content\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div class=\"content-container\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><main class=\"main\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div style=\"position:relative;\" class=\"vp-doc _smartclass-dispatchub_guide_api-usage\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\"><div><h1 id=\"api-usage\" tabindex=\"-1\">API Usage <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#api-usage\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;API Usage&quot;\">​</a></h1><p>This walkthrough follows one term from CSV upload to downloadable artifacts, then every mid-session control call. All calls sit under <code>/api/v1</code>, take <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;teamusers access token&gt;</code> and follow the permission rules in <a href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/permissions\">Permissions and access control</a>. Lists are wrapped in <code>{\"items\": [...]}</code> and errors are RFC 9457 problem details with a stable <code>detail</code> code.</p><p>Throughout, <code>$BASE_URL</code> is the service listen address (<code>http://127.0.0.1:8081</code> locally) and <code>$TOKEN</code> is a teamusers access token.</p><h2 id=\"import-a-timetable\" tabindex=\"-1\">Import a timetable <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#import-a-timetable\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Import a timetable&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>The upload is <code>multipart/form-data</code> with the CSV part named <code>file</code>, at most 1 MiB and at most <code>DISPATCH_MAX_IMPORT_ROWS</code> rows. Validation is always available as a dry run:</p><div class=\"language-http vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">http</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">POST</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> /api/v1/timetable/imports?dry_run=true&amp;mode=replace</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D;\">Content-Type</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\"> multipart/form-data; boundary=...</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">file=@timetable.csv</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>mode</code> is <code>replace</code> (default) or <code>append</code>. The dry run writes only the <code>imports</code> row with <code>status='dry_run'</code> and normalizes nothing; it answers <code>200</code> with the batch plus a preview of what a commit would materialize:</p><div class=\"language-json vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">json</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"id\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"01J8Z9...\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"term_code\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"2026-FALL\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"mode\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"replace\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"filename\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"timetable.csv\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"sha256\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"...\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"row_count\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"ok_count\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"error_count\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"errors\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: [],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"status\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"dry_run\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"imported_by\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"01J8Z8USER...\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"preview\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">    {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"row\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">2</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"course_code\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"CS101\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"session_count\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">16</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"first_starts_at\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"2026-09-07T08:00:00+08:00\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"last_ends_at\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"2026-12-21T09:40:00+08:00\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">  ]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">}</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Rules the validator enforces, row by row:</p><ul><li>the header row is required and matched <strong>by name in any order</strong>; unknown or missing columns are rejected;</li><li>the term exists and its <code>periods</code> cover <code>period_start..period_end</code>;</li><li><code>room_code</code> is bound and enabled;</li><li><code>weeks</code> is within <code>1..terms.weeks</code>;</li><li>no two rows of the same import overlap on <code>(room_code, weekday, period range, weeks)</code>;</li><li>a teacher double-booked across rooms is a <strong>warning</strong>: it is reported in <code>errors</code>/<code>error_count</code> but never rejects the file.</li></ul><p>Any blocking row error answers <code>422</code> with the problem detail <code>import_validation_failed</code> and an extra <code>errors</code> array carrying the blocking errors plus any warnings, and the batch is stored with <code>status='failed'</code> and <code>ok_count=0</code> - there is no partial commit. On a successful dry run or commit <code>ok_count</code> is the accepted row count and <code>error_count</code> counts only the warnings. Repeating the call without <code>dry_run=true</code> commits in one transaction and answers <code>201</code> with the import: the batch, the <code>schedule_entries</code> and the materialized <code>sessions</code>. In <code>replace</code> mode the term's previous entries are first marked <code>superseded_by = &lt;new import id&gt;</code> and their future <code>planned</code> sessions are canceled (<code>status='canceled'</code>); sessions already <code>recording</code> or <code>completed</code> are never touched. Concurrent imports for one term serialize on an advisory lock. Re-uploading the identical file (same SHA-256, same term) answers <code>409 duplicate_import</code> unless you add <code>?force=true</code>.</p><h2 id=\"sessions-materialize-from-the-rows\" tabindex=\"-1\">Sessions materialize from the rows <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#sessions-materialize-from-the-rows\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Sessions materialize from the rows&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>Each accepted row is expanded over <code>weeks × (weekday, period_start..period_end)</code> into one <code>sessions</code> row:</p><div class=\"language-text vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">text</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>date(week, weekday) = week1_monday + (week - 1) * 7 + (weekday - 1) days</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>starts_at = date + periods[period_start].start_time   in DISPATCH_TIMEZONE</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>ends_at   = date + periods[period_end].end_time       in DISPATCH_TIMEZONE</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Occurrences already in the past when the import commits are stored with <code>status='canceled'</code> (kept for the record) instead of <code>planned</code>. A collision with an existing live <strong>or planned</strong> recording on the same <code>(device_id, camera_enum)</code> is reported as the blocking row error <code>session_collision</code>, so the whole batch fails cleanly instead of double-booking a camera. In <code>mode=replace</code> the batch's own term is excluded from that check, because the commit supersedes its pending sessions; <code>mode=append</code> still collides with them.</p><p>Query the result:</p><div class=\"language-http vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">http</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">GET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> /api/v1/sessions?term_code=2026-FALL&amp;room_code=A301&amp;status=planned</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Filters are <code>term_code</code>, <code>room_code</code>, <code>date</code> (<code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>), <code>status</code>, <code>course_code</code> and <code>limit</code>; results are newest <code>starts_at</code> first. <code>date</code> matches a UTC calendar day against <code>starts_at</code> (<code>[00:00, next 00:00) UTC</code>), independent of <code>DISPATCH_TIMEZONE</code> (an unparsable date is rejected with <code>400 invalid_request</code>), and <code>course_code</code> only matches scheduled sessions - manual sessions have no entry to match. <code>limit</code> defaults to <code>100</code>, values above <code>1000</code> are clamped to <code>1000</code>, and a non-numeric or non-positive value answers <code>400 invalid_request</code>. <code>GET /api/v1/sessions/{id}</code> returns the session plus its photo ledger and the live upstream status.</p><h2 id=\"scheduled-recording-no-calls-needed\" tabindex=\"-1\">Scheduled recording, no calls needed <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#scheduled-recording-no-calls-needed\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Scheduled recording, no calls needed&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>A <code>planned</code> session is picked up by the scheduler <code>DISPATCH_PRESTART</code> (default <code>2m</code>) before <code>starts_at</code>. It transitions <code>planned → starting → recording</code> while the <code>stream_id</code> returned by webcam-server is stored on the row, then <code>recording → stopping → completed</code> around <code>ends_at</code> (plus <code>DISPATCH_POSTSTOP_GRACE</code>). If the device is flaky the start is retried up to <code>DISPATCH_START_RETRY_MAX</code> times; if the window closes without a start, the session becomes <code>missed</code>. See <a href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/operations\">Operations</a> for the full semantics.</p><h2 id=\"fetch-artifacts\" tabindex=\"-1\">Fetch artifacts <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#fetch-artifacts\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Fetch artifacts&quot;\">​</a></h2><div class=\"language-http vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">http</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">GET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> /api/v1/sessions/{id}/artifacts</span></span></code></pre></div><div class=\"language-json vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">json</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"stream_id\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"01J8Z4W3K5M7Q9R1T3V5X7Z9B1\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"status\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"completed\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"segments\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">    {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"segment_seq\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"size_bytes\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">73400320</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"duration_ms\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">30000</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"download_url\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"https://files.example.com/files/...?expires=...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">  ],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">  \"photos\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">    {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"photo_id\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"01J8Z5PHOTO000000000000000\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"taken_at\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"2026-09-07T00:05:12Z\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;\">      \"download_url\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;\">\"https://files.example.com/files/...?expires=...\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">  ]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\">}</span></span></code></pre></div><p>dispatchub does not mirror segment rows: they are re-derived from the recorded <code>stream_id</code>, and the download URLs are minted live by webcam-server with a <strong>15-minute TTL</strong> - never cache or persist them. A <code>stream_id</code> with no segments yet returns the session's current upstream status with an empty list.</p><h2 id=\"mid-session-control\" tabindex=\"-1\">Mid-session control <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#mid-session-control\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Mid-session control&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>All five control calls share the same envelope: they accept an optional <code>X-Idempotency-Key</code> header, log the caller (<code>actor_id</code> = token subject) and every outcome into <code>camera_commands</code>, and translate upstream failures into the stable error codes below. Replaying a request with the same idempotency key returns the stored outcome instead of issuing a second upstream command.</p><table tabindex=\"0\"><thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/recording/start</code></td><td>Manual start of a <code>planned</code> session - early start, or a re-start after <code>failed</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/sessions/{id}/recording/stop</code></td><td>Manual stop of that session.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/recording/start</code></td><td>Ad-hoc start; creates a <code>manual</code> session for the room.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/recording/stop</code></td><td>Ad-hoc stop of the room's live session.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/camera/switch</code></td><td><code>{\"camera_enum\": N}</code> mid-session camera switch.</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/photo</code></td><td>Snapshot; answered with <code>{\"session_photo_id\", \"request_id\", \"status\": \"pending\"}</code>.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Response statuses: session start/stop and the ad-hoc room stop answer <code>200</code> with the session; the ad-hoc room start answers <code>201</code> with the new <code>manual</code> session and <code>Location: /api/v1/sessions/{id}</code>; camera switch answers <code>202</code> with <code>{\"command_id\", \"camera_enum\"}</code>; the snapshot answers <code>202</code> with the pending body above.</p><p>Snapshot ids are asynchronous: <code>POST …/photo</code> only starts the capture upstream, and webcam-server returns the id later. dispatchub stores a <code>session_photos</code> row and polls <code>GET /api/devices/{device_id}/photos</code>, matching on <code>request_id</code> until it can persist the real <code>photo_id</code> (status <code>resolved</code>). If the TTL (<code>DISPATCH_PHOTO_POLL_TTL</code>, default <code>15m</code>) passes without a match the row becomes <code>unresolved</code>; it is retried with a growing backoff, so an upstream outage degrades into lag rather than a hot loop. A snapshot while the room is idle is legal and produces a row with no session.</p><p>The current state of a room is proxied live:</p><div class=\"language-http vp-adaptive-theme\"><button title=\"Copy Code\" class=\"copy\"></button><span class=\"lang\">http</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;\">GET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;\"> /api/v1/rooms/{room_code}/live</span></span></code></pre></div><p>answers <code>{online, cameras: [...], active_session: {id, stream_id, started_at}}</code> from webcam-server.</p><h2 id=\"stable-error-codes\" tabindex=\"-1\">Stable error codes <a class=\"header-anchor\" href=\"#stable-error-codes\" aria-label=\"Permalink to &quot;Stable error codes&quot;\">​</a></h2><p>Errors are <code>application/problem+json</code>; switch on the <code>detail</code> string:</p><table tabindex=\"0\"><thead><tr><th><code>detail</code></th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>invalid_request</code></td><td>Malformed body, query or path.</td></tr><tr><td><code>invalid_token</code></td><td>The bearer token failed local verification.</td></tr><tr><td><code>permission denied</code></td><td>Verified caller, no candidate <code>dispatch:*</code> key allowed.</td></tr><tr><td><code>term_not_found</code></td><td>The referenced term does not exist.</td></tr><tr><td><code>periods_not_configured</code></td><td>The term has no 节次 table configured, or a request uses a period it does not cover.</td></tr><tr><td><code>room_not_bound</code></td><td>The room has no binding (or it is disabled).</td></tr><tr><td><code>device_not_found</code></td><td>webcam-server does not know the bound device.</td></tr><tr><td><code>session_not_found</code></td><td>The session does not exist.</td></tr><tr><td><code>session_not_planned</code></td><td>The manual start target is not in a state that can start.</td></tr><tr><td><code>already_streaming</code></td><td>A stream is already active on that device/camera (adopted by the scheduler, rejected for manual calls).</td></tr><tr><td><code>device_offline</code></td><td>webcam-server reports the device offline.</td></tr><tr><td><code>no_active_stream</code></td><td>The stop target has no live stream upstream.</td></tr><tr><td><code>upstream_unavailable</code></td><td>webcam-server could not be reached or answered 502.</td></tr><tr><td><code>duplicate_idempotency_key</code></td><td>The <code>X-Idempotency-Key</code> collides with a different command.</td></tr><tr><td><code>duplicate_import</code></td><td>The identical CSV was already imported for the term.</td></tr><tr><td><code>session_collision</code></td><td>An imported row overlaps an existing live or planned recording on the same device/camera.</td></tr><tr><td><code>room_has_history</code></td><td>The room is referenced by timetable or session history; disable it (<code>PUT</code> with <code>\"enabled\": false</code>) instead of deleting it.</td></tr><tr><td><code>import_validation_failed</code></td><td>One or more CSV rows failed validation; the full list is in the batch.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><code>401</code> responses carry the teamusers decision body (<code>{\"allow\": false, \"reason\": \"...\"}</code>) instead of a problem detail; an IAM outage answers <code>503</code> and never allows the request. See the <a href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/api/overview\">API reference</a> for the per-route statuses.</p></div></div></main><footer class=\"VPDocFooter\" data-v-a3d537d1=\"\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><!--[--><!--]--><div class=\"edit-info\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><!----><div class=\"last-updated\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><p class=\"VPLastUpdated\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\" data-v-3104ff47=\"\">Last updated: <time datetime=\"2026-10-05T12:46:33.000Z\" data-v-3104ff47=\"\"></time></p></div></div><nav class=\"prev-next\" aria-labelledby=\"doc-footer-aria-label\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><span class=\"visually-hidden\" id=\"doc-footer-aria-label\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Pager</span><div class=\"pager\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><a class=\"VPLink link pager-link prev\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/permissions\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><!--[--><span class=\"desc\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Previous page</span><span class=\"title\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Permissions</span><!--]--></a></div><div class=\"pager\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><a class=\"VPLink link pager-link next\" href=\"/smartclass-dispatchub/guide/operations\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\"><!--[--><span class=\"desc\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Next page</span><span class=\"title\" data-v-aace3ab5=\"\">Operations</span><!--]--></a></div></nav></footer><!--[--><!--]--></div></div></div><!--[--><!--]--></div></div><!----><!--[--><!--]--></div></div>\n    <script>window.__VP_HASH_MAP__=JSON.parse(\"{\\\"api_overview.md\\\":\\\"DAAwgvcA\\\",\\\"api_reference_health.md\\\":\\\"BY1TgOb0\\\",\\\"api_reference_re